ly in the beginning showing  michael his dad  played by brian cranston on his run he  even stops at his wife's grave  but he makes a stop at this house  in this poor neighborhood and it's  actually the house that has directly to  do with the case  he is handling as a judge and this is  just to show you how honorable of a  judge  he is looking for the truth in all ways  and it's completely just to go  that far to check on that case but  before we get back to michael  we see with adam that he's asthmatic  which is super important  and is really a big variable in all  these events that take place so  where stuff starts at the fan with adam  as he brings his mother's photo to this  yaya's food store in this bad  neighborhood clearly the spot his mother  died but  you see there's like this gang that  comes up to him and he wants to get out  of there he starts panicking his asthma  starts kicking up  but what's even crazier is there's a car  following him so that's what's causing  him to drive really fast and not focus  clearly and eventually into him hitting  in this motorcycle  and he can't reach his inhaler but  that's a little another thing you got to  pay attention to is that  when he hits this motorcycle the car  that was following him was still there  sees what happened completely but turns  around and leaves a scene that's also  going to be very important who was in  that car what was the eyewitness  the most frustrating thing about this  character in adam is that the minute he  hit the kid  on the motorcycle he doesn't first go  and grab his inhaler in the car  he first goes and checks on the kid and  this is just so  frustrating to watch because he's having  this asthma attack but also panicking so  that when he actually  uses the kid's phone to call the police  he doesn't just open his mouth and tell  them what happened  so you could tell yeah he's in shock but  you find yourself screaming at the  screen at this kid but again more little  important things like 